From: SK-18 open firmware <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_hid: queue 1024 OUT reports instead of 4

The SK-18 carries its deck protocol in 512-byte HID reports. A 58 KB frame
is about 115 reports back to back. f_hid queues only 4 receive requests,
which is the same problem as with u_serial (see the u_serial patch): the
sunxi musb controller has a packet in its FIFO with no request to put it
in once the queue runs dry, and packets go missing. Queueing 1024 requests
(512 KB) keeps the queue from running dry during a burst.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c	2026-11-10 10:04:32.384955706 -0600
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/f_hid.c	2026-11-10 10:04:32.391934758 -0600
@@ -1653,7 +1653,7 @@
 	hidg->func.free_func = hidg_free;
 
 	/* this could be made configurable at some point */
-	hidg->qlen	   = 4;
+	hidg->qlen	   = 1024;
 
 	return &hidg->func;
 
